<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea seeks 55,000 tonnes of No.1 soybean.</title>
<headline>S.Korea seeks 55,000 tonnes of No.1 soybean.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's state-run Agricultural &amp; Fishery Marketing Corp (AFMC) said on Thursday it would invite tenders for 55,000 tonnes of No.1 soybean on December 4.  </p>
<p>An official at the corporation said it will accept the bids until 4:00 p.m. (0800 GMT). The bids will be opened on December 5.</p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follow:</p>
<p> POSITION  TONNE	     SHIPMENT		   ARRIVAL/PORT</p>
<p>			  U.S. GULF	U.S. PNW</p>
<p>  ONE     30,000    Dec 6-25	 Dec 21-Jan 10  Jan 30/Inchon</p>
<p>  TWO     25,000    Dec 26-Jan 15  Jan 11-30	Feb 20/Inchon</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
